                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Mindware has once again brought back to life yet another forgotten 1980's classic. \n\n● First was \"地底最大の作戦\" by Takaya Arita in 1980 which became COSMIC CAVERN 3671\n● Next was \"SPACE MOUSE\" by Takanari Suzuki in 1981\n● And now \"MR. JONG\" by Kiwako in 1983 has been turned into ACTION MAHJONG\n\nThe game is in early access, but there are still plenty of differences from its predecessor. The four demons from MR. JONG have been replaced by 3 Mahjong players and 1 demon. Also there's a local multi-player mode.\n\nHopefully SHARP MZ-80 and NEC PC styles will be added. Steam cards would be nice too.\n\nEven though the game is mostly in Japanese, it's simple enough for anyone to understand. Knowledge of Japanese Mahjong is still a must though.",
